      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-thmblue mb-4">
        Renormalised PT-Buchstab equation<span class="inline-flex items-center px-2 py-0.5 rounded text-[10px] font-bold uppercase tracking-wider bg-thmblue/10 text-thmblue ml-2 align-middle">PT contribution</span>
      </h2>
      <div class="text-slate-700 leading-relaxed space-y-4">
        <p>
          The programme starts from the classical Buchstab function
          $\omega(u)$ — defined by $\omega(u) = 1/u$ for $u \in [1, 2]$ and
          {String.raw`$(u\omega(u))' = \omega(u-1)$`} for {String.raw`$u > 2$`}
          — then introduces the renormalised ratio.
        </p>
        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
          <div class="bg-white border border-slate-200 rounded-lg p-5">
            <h3 class="font-sans font-semibold text-thmblue mb-2 text-sm">BR1 — Exact prime-step transport</h3>
            <div class="bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200 rounded p-3 font-mono text-sm overflow-x-auto">
              {String.raw`$\Phi_a(x) = \Phi_{a-1}(x) - \Phi_{a-1}\!\left(\lfloor x/p_a \rfloor\right)$`}
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-white border border-slate-200 rounded-lg p-5">
            <h3 class="font-sans font-semibold text-thmblue mb-2 text-sm">BR2 — Renormalised transport</h3>
            <div class="bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200 rounded p-3 font-mono text-xs overflow-x-auto">
              {String.raw`$R_a(x) = \dfrac{R_{a-1}(x) - (\lfloor x/p_a \rfloor / x)\,R_{a-1}(\lfloor x/p_a \rfloor)}{1 - 1/p_a}$`}
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-amber-50 border border-amber-300 rounded-lg p-5 mt-4">
          <h3 class="font-sans font-semibold text-amber-900 mb-2">BR4 — Candidate PT kernel</h3>
          <div class="bg-white/70 border border-amber-200 rounded p-3 font-mono text-sm">
            {String.raw`$K_{PT}(u) = e^\gamma \omega(u), \qquad u = \log x / \log y$`}
          </div>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-700 mt-3">
            At the square-root point $u = 2$:
            {String.raw`$K_{PT}(2) = e^\gamma / 2 \approx 0.8905$`}.
            Numerical validation at $x = 10^6$: exact ratio
            {String.raw`$0.9675$`}, relative factor {String.raw`$1.086$`};
            at $u = 4$, agreement to within {String.raw`$10^{-4}$`}.
            Status: <strong>universal candidate</strong>, open programme.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    {/* ═════════════════════════ L3 — THETA GAP LAW ═════════════════════════ */}
    <section data-min-depth="L3" class="mb-14">
      <span class="pt-tag pt-tag-cond mb-3 inline-block">Technical · PT contribution</span>
